{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C9tJTUhFD3BnGryGSoKo9K","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026)\n5\t\n6\t## Paper Type\n7\tEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n8\t\n9\t## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n10\t\n11\t**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n12\t- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%)\n13\t- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n14\t- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n15\t\n16\t**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n17\t- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n18\t- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\"\n19\t\n20\t**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n21\t- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n22\t- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n23\t- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n24\t\n25\t**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n26\t1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n27\t2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n28\t3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n29\t4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n30\t- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n31\t- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n32\t- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n33\t- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n34\t\n35\t## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n36\t\n37\t**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n38\t\n39\t**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n40\t\n41\t**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n42\t\n43\t1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n44\t\n45\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n46\t\n47\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n48\t\n49\t4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n50\t\n51\t**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n52\t\n53\t## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n54\t\n55\t**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n56\t- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n57\t- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n58\t- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n59\t- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n60\t- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n61\t- §6 Conclusion\n62\t\n63\t**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n64\t- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n65\t- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n66\t- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n67\t- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n68\t- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n69\t- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n70\t- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n71\t- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n72\t\n73\t## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n74\t\n75\tSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n76\t\n77\t## Venue Fit\n78\t\n79\t- **ICLR 2027**: Good fit — empirical analysis of evaluation methodology, psychometric rigor, large-scale characterization. Risk: ML reviewers may not be familiar with DIF/IRT. Mitigation: §3 provides self-contained DIF primer with ML translations.\n80\t\n81\t## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n82\t\n83\tMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n84\t\n85\t1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n86\t\n87\t2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n88\t\n89\t3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n90\t\n91\t**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n92\t\n93\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n94\t\n95\t1. **\"38% could just mean models got better\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%). Subject-level ρ=0.307 is an ecological correlation that grossly overstates the item-level relationship (pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Present Model 1 (2.4pp) as primary; acknowledge confounder-vs-mediator ambiguity in Model 2 as honest discussion.\n96\t\n97\t2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n98\t\n99\t3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n100\t\n101\t4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n102\t\n103\t5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n104\t\n105\t6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n106\t\n107\t7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n108\t\n109\t8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n110\t\n111\t9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n112\t\n113\t10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n114\t\n115\t11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n116\t\n117\t## Dropped from Original Framing\n118\t\n119\t- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n120\t- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n121\t- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n122\t- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n123\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c6b9965-4730-46a2-a3a4-07c965d9e09e","uuid":"8641069b-bf5f-4e62-8304-647a355fe67e","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:44:30.081Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T062008/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026)\n\n## Paper Type\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\" not \"DIF detects contamination.\"\n\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\n\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement), plan_022 (model independence: graduated de-duplication to 1 model per family → C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap K; K=20: 29.1% vs random 30.9%, K=5: 11.7% vs random 16.9%; family structure does NOT inflate C%)\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\n\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\n- Framing: aggressive — \"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\"\n\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\n\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations,\" not \"good items.\"\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \"find bad items and remove\" but \"understand what changed and why.\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587. **Item characterization** (plan_023): DIF-C items are moderately harder (Cohen's d=-0.247) and higher-discrimination (d=0.230) than non-DIF items, but uniformly distributed across MMLU domains (χ² p=0.32). Key finding: difficulty × DIF direction interaction (ρ=-0.597) — hardest-decile DIF-C items are 88.7% focal-favoring (2024 models do better), easiest-decile are 96.2% reference-favoring (2023 models do better). This reveals a systematic pattern: capability improvement concentrates on hard items, while easy items' difficulty structure erodes across generations.\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33), plan_023 (item characterization: difficulty ρ=-0.597, domain uniformity χ² p=0.32)\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\n- Growing Pains互补: \"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\"\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\n\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\n\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\n\n**Key narrative principle**: \"Instability ≠ invalidity.\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\n\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\n\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \"models got better.\"\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\n\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\n\n**Headline result**: \"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\"\n\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\n\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \"instability ≠ invalidity\" framing upfront)\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\n- §6 Conclusion\n\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\n\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\n\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\n\n## Venue Fit\n\n- **ICLR 2027**: Good fit — empirical analysis of evaluation methodology, psychometric rigor, large-scale characterization. Risk: ML reviewers may not be familiar with DIF/IRT. Mitigation: §3 provides self-contained DIF primer with ML translations.\n\n## Novelty Articulation (三层，显式化)\n\nMH-DIF (1959/1988) is applied without modification. **Explicitly acknowledge this.** Novelty is NOT algorithmic. Three layers of genuine contribution:\n\n1. **Empirical discovery at unprecedented scale**: First DIF analysis on 5,227×12,508 LLM response matrix. Finding: 31% temporal instability is robust across thresholds (10-49%), not explained by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and architecturally homogeneous (99.98% decoder-only). No prior work has characterized item-level stability of LLM benchmarks at this scale. The instability finding itself is new data about MMLU's measurement properties.\n\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique with field-wide implications**: The observation that web-overlap labels cannot validate item-level differential detectors is NOT obvious — the field routinely uses them. This affects the validity claims of Min-K%, ConStat, n-gram methods, and all papers using web-overlap as ground truth. First empirical demonstration (enrichment≈1.0 + semi-synthetic proof).\n\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework + cross-subject matching**: The ΔTPR methodology is a reusable infrastructure contribution. Cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000) is a novel practical innovation — the insight that within-subject matching contaminates the conditioning variable is subtle and general. Portable to any multi-domain benchmark (demonstrated on GSM8K).\n\n**Framing**: \"We bring mature psychometric tools to characterize an urgent ML evaluation problem. The contribution is the empirical findings, the validation methodology critique, and the reusable framework — not a new algorithm.\"\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns (updated for pivot)\n\n1. **\"38% could just mean models got better\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_019). Item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%). Subject-level ρ=0.307 is an ecological correlation that grossly overstates the item-level relationship (pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Present Model 1 (2.4pp) as primary; acknowledge confounder-vs-mediator ambiguity in Model 2 as honest discussion.\n\n2. **\"Ground truth critique is obvious — of course web labels don't capture differential effects\"** — Not obvious: the field routinely uses these labels for item-level validation. We provide the first empirical demonstration with both the enrichment≈1.0 result and the semi-synthetic proof of concept.\n\n3. **\"Semi-synthetic injection is artificial\"** — We inject into real response matrices (not simulated), preserving real ability distributions and item characteristics. The mechanism (incorrect→correct flipping) is a simplification acknowledged in limitations.\n\n4. **\"DIF power is only sufficient for large effects\"** — Large effects are precisely what threaten benchmark validity most. Operational region: N≥80, δ≥1.4, TPR=0.68-0.80.\n\n5. **\"Only validated on MMLU\"** — Partially addressed: GSM8K replication (METABENCH 1,319 items × 6,702 models) confirms semi-synthetic framework portability (ΔTPR=+0.818) and temporal DIF pattern (C%=18.9%). GSM1K contamination gap validation (N=33) provides cross-benchmark evidence. Full generalization to diverse benchmarks remains future work.\n\n6. **\"Higher methods (MIMIC, propensity-score) could solve the confounding\"** — Acknowledged as future work. We frame our three-attempt negative results as \"empirical observation\" that motivates these directions, not as impossibility.\n\n7. **\"ETS threshold is uncalibrated for LLM populations\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). C% at {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} = {48.9%, 31.3%, 18.3%, 10.2%}. Finding >15% holds at standard thresholds [1.0, 2.0]. At conservative 2.5, still 10.2% (1,278 items). Present as: \"finding is robust across standard thresholds; even at the most conservative cutoff, >10% of items show large DIF.\" Do NOT claim \">15% at all thresholds\" — be honest that 2.5 drops below.\n\n8. **\"Multiple testing: 12,508 simultaneous tests without correction\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_018). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 removes only 3/3,918 ETS C items (31.32%→31.30%). At higher thresholds, BH impact is zero. ETS dual requirement (effect size + significance) provides near-complete implicit protection. Random-split sanity check (C%=0.18%) confirms empirically.\n\n9. **\"Only uniform DIF — non-uniform DIF plausible for LLMs\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_021). LR-DIF on 9 subjects (1787 items): MH C-class 92.1% concordance with LR uniform DIF → MH detection robust. Non-uniform DIF: 38.7% at significance threshold, **24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5** (conservative, effect-size controlled). MH structurally underestimates instability. Caveat: LR used within-subject matching (vs MH's cross-benchmark), so 38.7% may be inflated; use 24.8% in paper. Framing: \"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative.\"\n\n10. **\"5,227 models are not independent — fine-tunes/merges inflate N and DIF significance\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_022). Graduated de-duplication (capping models per family at K=1,2,5,10,20) shows C% ≤ random subsample control at every cap: K=20 (447 models) C%=29.1% vs random 30.9%; K=5 (146 models) C%=11.7% vs random 16.9%; K=1 (33 families) C%=0.17% (underpowered, N<80). Family structure does NOT inflate C% — if anything, de-duplication reduces it slightly less than random subsampling. The 31.3% figure is robust to model non-independence.\n\n11. **\"Ranking disruption result is tautological\"** — ✅ RESOLVED (plan_020). Circularity ablation shows DIF removal is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157, discrimination z=-16, variance z=-108. Despite 62.6% item overlap with accuracy-gap selection, MH ability conditioning makes DIF 10-16× less disruptive. DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just items with large raw group differences. Tautology refuted.\n\n## Dropped from Original Framing\n\n- **Ensemble (Claim 2 old)**: plan_003a/b/c never executed. Future work.\n- **Regeneration (Claim 3 old)**: Bifactor killed by plan_014 pre-check. Dropped entirely.\n- **RL robustness**: Theoretically motivated but N=13 insufficient. Limitations disclosure, not claim.\n- **Detection as primary contribution**: Pivoted from \"we detect contamination\" to \"we characterize benchmark properties.\"\n","numLines":123,"startLine":1,"totalLines":123}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WA5tJZ4gqg6JPWwfmRV74V","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"METABENCH MMLU 全量 DIF 分析。temporal/ability/within-family 三种 cohort 定义， 加 Li et al. proxy validation 和 domain specificity。\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n7\t      \"temporal_n_c_items\": 3918,\n8\t      \"temporal_n_total\": 12508,\n9\t      \"temporal_fpr_on_li_clean\": 0.318,\n10\t      \"temporal_enrichment_ratio\": 0.96,\n11\t      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n12\t      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n13\t      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n14\t      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n15\t      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n16\t      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n17\t      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n18\t      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n19\t    },\n20\t    \"tables\": [\n21\t      {\n22\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary by ETS Classification\",\n23\t        \"columns\": [\n24\t          \"ets_class\",\n25\t          \"n_items\",\n26\t          \"pct\",\n27\t          \"mean_abs_delta_mh\"\n28\t        ],\n29\t        \"rows\": [\n30\t          [\n31\t            \"A (negligible)\",\n32\t            8590,\n33\t            68.7,\n34\t            0.43\n35\t          ],\n36\t          [\n37\t            \"B (moderate)\",\n38\t            2641,\n39\t            21.1,\n40\t            1.24\n41\t          ],\n42\t          [\n43\t            \"C (large)\",\n44\t            1277,\n45\t            10.2,\n46\t            2.31\n47\t          ],\n48\t          [\n49\t            \"B+C (flagged)\",\n50\t            3918,\n51\t            31.3,\n52\t            1.58\n53\t          ]\n54\t        ]\n55\t      },\n56\t      {\n57\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Cohort Definition Sensitivity\",\n58\t        \"columns\": [\n59\t          \"cohort\",\n60\t          \"n_ref\",\n61\t          \"n_foc\",\n62\t          \"c_pct\",\n63\t          \"enrichment\"\n64\t        ],\n65\t        \"rows\": [\n66\t          [\n67\t            \"temporal (2023 vs 2024-H1)\",\n68\t            1253,\n69\t            656,\n70\t            31.3,\n71\t            0.96\n72\t          ],\n73\t          [\n74\t            \"ability (Q1 vs Q5)\",\n75\t            \"~1044\",\n76\t            \"~1044\",\n77\t            2.9,\n78\t            1.19\n79\t          ],\n80\t          [\n81\t            \"within-family (Llama-2 vs 3)\",\n82\t            161,\n83\t            308,\n84\t            61.3,\n85\t            \"—\"\n86\t          ],\n87\t          [\n88\t            \"random split (sanity)\",\n89\t            950,\n90\t            950,\n91\t            0.18,\n92\t            \"—\"\n93\t          ]\n94\t        ]\n95\t      }\n96\t    ],\n97\t    \"figures\": [],\n98\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_001 是 paper 的基石。数据本身不受质疑，但 \\\"so what\\\" 需要后续实验 (plan_019, plan_017, plan_020) 支撑。评审预期反应： R1: \\\"Impressive scale, but what does 31% instability mean for practitioners?\\\" R2: \\\"The enrichment≈1.0 result is interesting but undermines the contamination framing\\\" R3: \\\"Within-family results suggest capability gain, not contamination\\\" 总体：plan_001 在 median 档得 strong accept 作为 empirical contribution， 但单独不够——需要 downstream impact story。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档下这些数值本身站得住——31.3% 是 robust 的经验发现，random-split sanity (0.18%) 排除统计伪影， domain ρ=0.307 是 modest ecological correlation。问题不在数字，在解读： 1) enrichment≈1.0 证明 DIF 和 web-overlap labels 正交，但评审会问 \\\"if DIF doesn't correlate with known contamination, what IS it detecting?\\\"——需要 plan_019 decomposition 才能回答 \\\"item-specific instability, not capability gain\\\"。 2) within-family C%=61.3% (Llama-2 vs 3) 远高于 cross-cohort 31.3%，评审会质疑 \\\"within-family analysis proves capability gain drives DIF, not contamination\\\"。 Median 档下 1 个评审接受 \\\"capability gain ≠ item instability\\\" 论证，1 个不接受。 3) domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 在 median 档被视为 \\\"interesting but not definitive\\\"， 不被攻击也不加分。\\n\"\n99\t  },\n100\t  {\n101\t    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n102\t    \"description\": \"验证 DIF 在 RL-trained 模型上的鲁棒性。SFT baseline vs alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO) vs reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO)。关键在于 reasoning-RL 只有 10-15 个模型。\\n\",\n103\t    \"results\": {\n104\t      \"sft_cohort_n\": 312,\n105\t      \"alignment_rl_cohort_n\": 477,\n106\t      \"reasoning_rl_models_collected\": 13,\n107\t      \"sft_vs_alignment_jaccard_dif_flags\": 0.72,\n108\t      \"sft_temporal_c_pct\": 30.8,\n109\t      \"alignment_rl_temporal_c_pct\": 32.1,\n110\t      \"combined_with_reasoning_rl_c_pct\": 31.5,\n111\t      \"jaccard_base_vs_rl_augmented\": 0.91,\n112\t      \"tost_equivalence_p\": 0.14,\n113\t      \"tost_equivalence_bound\": 0.05,\n114\t      \"tost_verdict\": \"inconclusive\",\n115\t      \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.61,\n116\t      \"mink_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.58,\n117\t      \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.43,\n118\t      \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.64,\n119\t      \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.39,\n120\t      \"delong_p_mink_sft_vs_rl\": 0.08,\n121\t      \"delong_p_constat_sft_vs_rl\": 0.03,\n122\t      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_diff_mink\": [\n123\t        -0.02,\n124\t        0.38\n125\t      ],\n126\t      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_diff_constat\": [\n127\t        0.04,\n128\t        0.46\n129\t      ],\n130\t      \"power_analysis_delta_boundary\": 1.1,\n131\t      \"power_analysis_tpr_at_boundary\": 0.42\n132\t    },\n133\t    \"tables\": [\n134\t      {\n135\t        \"name\": \"Table: DIF Flag Stability Under Cohort Composition Change\",\n136\t        \"columns\": [\n137\t          \"cohort_composition\",\n138\t          \"n_total\",\n139\t          \"c_pct\",\n140\t          \"jaccard_vs_baseline\"\n141\t        ],\n142\t        \"rows\": [\n143\t          [\n144\t            \"SFT only\",\n145\t            312,\n146\t            30.8,\n147\t            \"—\"\n148\t          ],\n149\t          [\n150\t            \"SFT + alignment-RL\",\n151\t            789,\n152\t            32.1,\n153\t            0.72\n154\t          ],\n155\t          [\n156\t            \"SFT + alignment-RL + reasoning-RL\",\n157\t            802,\n158\t            31.5,\n159\t            0.91\n160\t          ]\n161\t        ]\n162\t      },\n163\t      {\n164\t        \"name\": \"Table: Individual Detector AUROC by Model Type\",\n165\t        \"columns\": [\n166\t          \"detector\",\n167\t          \"sft\",\n168\t          \"alignment_rl\",\n169\t          \"reasoning_rl\",\n170\t          \"delong_p\"\n171\t        ],\n172\t        \"rows\": [\n173\t          [\n174\t            \"Min-K%\",\n175\t            0.61,\n176\t            0.58,\n177\t            0.43,\n178\t            0.08\n179\t          ],\n180\t          [\n181\t            \"ConStat\",\n182\t            0.64,\n183\t            0.6,\n184\t            0.39,\n185\t            0.03\n186\t          ],\n187\t          [\n188\t            \"DIF (group)\",\n189\t            \"—\",\n190\t            \"—\",\n191\t            \"—\",\n192\t            \"N/A\"\n193\t          ]\n194\t        ]\n195\t      }\n196\t    ],\n197\t    \"figures\": [],\n198\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_002 是最弱的实验。N=13 reasoning-RL 无法支撑任何统计结论。 TOST inconclusive 意味着既不能声称 robust 也不能声称 fragile。 最佳策略：power analysis 图放 appendix，主文用一句话承认 \\\"reasoning-RL validation remains underpowered (N=13); alignment-RL cohort (N=477) shows stable DIF flags (Jaccard=0.72 vs SFT)\\\"。不把 RL robustness 作为 claim。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心问题：N=13 reasoning-RL 模型严重不足。 1) Group-level DIF flags 在加入 13 个 RL 模型后变化很小 (Jaccard=0.91)，因为 N=13 在 N≈1900 focal cohort 中占比 <1%，统计上几乎无影响。评审会正确指出 \\\"this doesn't prove RL robustness, it proves RL models are too few to matter\\\"。 2) TOST 等价性检验 p=0.14 不显著——无法证明等价，也无法证明差异。 Median 档评审判断：inconclusive，移至 limitations。 3) 个体模型检测：ConStat 在 reasoning-RL 上 AUROC 降至 0.39 (显著下降)， 但 DIF 是 group-level 无法做个体比较，comparison 不对等。 4) Power analysis 有理论价值：δ<1.1 时 TPR<0.42，清晰刻画了 detection boundary。 但评审会说 \\\"you characterized a limitation, not solved it\\\"。 总体：plan_002 在 median 档被降级为 appendix，N=13 是 fatal underpowering。\\n\"\n199\t  },\n200\t  {\n201\t    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n202\t    \"description\": \"独立评估 ConStat-style perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的检测力。 200+ items paraphrased，comparison with DIF flags。\\n\",\n203\t    \"results\": {\n204\t      \"n_items_paraphrased\": 217,\n205\t      \"paraphrase_quality_human_eval\": 0.78,\n206\t      \"constat_detection_rate_fdr005\": 0.23,\n207\t      \"constat_detection_rate_fdr010\": 0.31,\n208\t      \"constat_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.08,\n209\t      \"constat_fpr_on_clean_items\": 0.06,\n210\t      \"constat_effect_size_non_rl\": 0.74,\n211\t      \"constat_effect_size_rl\": 0.31,\n212\t      \"paraphrase_difficulty_shift_mean\": 0.12,\n213\t      \"paraphrase_difficulty_shift_std\": 0.34,\n214\t      \"n_models_tested\": 15,\n215\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 62\n216\t    },\n217\t    \"tables\": [\n218\t      {\n219\t        \"name\": \"Table: ConStat Detection Summary\",\n220\t        \"columns\": [\n221\t          \"metric\",\n222\t          \"non_rl_models\",\n223\t          \"rl_models\",\n224\t          \"all\"\n225\t        ],\n226\t        \"rows\": [\n227\t          [\n228\t            \"n_models\",\n229\t            11,\n230\t            4,\n231\t            15\n232\t          ],\n233\t          [\n234\t            \"detection_rate_fdr005\",\n235\t            0.27,\n236\t            0.14,\n237\t            0.23\n238\t          ],\n239\t          [\n240\t            \"mean_effect_size\",\n241\t            0.74,\n242\t            0.31,\n243\t            0.61\n244\t          ],\n245\t          [\n246\t            \"FPR\",\n247\t            0.05,\n248\t            0.08,\n249\t            0.06\n250\t          ]\n251\t        ]\n252\t      }\n253\t    ],\n254\t    \"figures\": [],\n255\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_003a 提供了有价值的 baseline comparison，但不构成独立贡献。 ConStat-DIF orthogonality (Jaccard=0.08) 支持 meta-critique (不同方法 capture 不同 aspects)，但 N=15 模型限制了结论强度。适合 appendix 作为 related work empirical comparison，不适合 main body。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：ConStat 实验执行了但结果 mixed。 1) Paraphrase 质量 78% human-eval acceptable——约 22% 的 reformulation 引入了 subtle semantic shift，导致 difficulty 变化不纯粹来自 contamination。 评审会质疑 paraphrase 质量是 confound。 2) FDR-controlled detection rate 23% 在 non-RL 模型上——reasonable baseline 但 不 impressive。Jaccard=0.08 与 DIF 几乎无 overlap，说明两者 detect 不同 signal。 3) RL 模型上 effect size 从 0.74 降至 0.31——方向正确但 N=15 模型下 CI 非常宽。 4) 核心问题：ConStat 需要 inference access (running paraphrased items through models)， 而 METABENCH 只有 original responses。所以 ConStat 只在 15 个有 inference access 的模型上跑，vs DIF 用全部 5,227 模型。Scale 不可比。 Median 档评审判断：\\\"useful baseline comparison but limited by small inference sample\\\"。\\n\"\n256\t  },\n257\t  {\n258\t    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n259\t    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的独立评估。50 responses/item via temperature sampling。\\n\",\n260\t    \"results\": {\n261\t      \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n262\t      \"n_items_tested\": 500,\n263\t      \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n264\t      \"temperature\": 0.8,\n265\t      \"bimodal_detection_rate\": 0.14,\n266\t      \"bimodal_verbatim_contamination\": 0.31,\n267\t      \"bimodal_variant_contamination\": 0.06,\n268\t      \"dvd_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.05,\n269\t      \"dvd_fpr\": 0.09,\n270\t      \"variance_score_reliability\": 0.62,\n271\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 58\n272\t    },\n273\t    \"tables\": [\n274\t      {\n275\t        \"name\": \"Table: DVD Detection by Contamination Type\",\n276\t        \"columns\": [\n277\t          \"contamination_type\",\n278\t          \"n_items_tested\",\n279\t          \"bimodal_rate\",\n280\t          \"fpr\"\n281\t        ],\n282\t        \"rows\": [\n283\t          [\n284\t            \"verbatim\",\n285\t            150,\n286\t            0.31,\n287\t            0.08\n288\t          ],\n289\t          [\n290\t            \"variant\",\n291\t            150,\n292\t            0.06,\n293\t            0.1\n294\t          ],\n295\t          [\n296\t            \"clean\",\n297\t            200,\n298\t            \"—\",\n299\t            0.09\n300\t          ]\n301\t        ]\n302\t      }\n303\t    ],\n304\t    \"figures\": [],\n305\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_003b 是最弱的独立实验。Detection power 低于 ConStat， 且需要 open-weight inference access。主要价值是证明 \\\"generation variance alone is insufficient\\\"——但这不是 surprising finding。Appendix material at best。 在 median 档的策略调整中，plan_003b 应被 deprioritized。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：DVD 结果较弱。 1) 只有 14% 的 items 显示 bimodal generation variance——远低于 DIF 的 31.3%， 说明 generation variance 作为 contamination signal 灵敏度较低。 2) Verbatim contamination (31% bimodal) vs variant contamination (6% bimodal)： DVD 几乎只能 detect verbatim memorization，对 variant 无力。 3) 与 DIF 的 overlap 近乎为零 (Jaccard=0.05)，再次说明不同方法 capture 不同 signal。 4) Variance score reliability 0.62——moderate at best。50 responses 可能不足以 稳定估计 variance，但 GPU budget 已耗尽。 5) 核心限制：DVD 需要 open-weight + inference，排除 closed-source models。 Median 档评审：\\\"limited detection power, primarily captures verbatim memorization which is already detectable by simpler methods (n-gram matching)\\\"。\\n\"\n306\t  },\n307\t  {\n308\t    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n309\t    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号 ensemble。依赖 003a 和 003b。\\n\",\n310\t    \"results\": {\n311\t      \"ensemble_auroc_2of3\": 0.58,\n312\t      \"ensemble_auroc_weighted\": 0.62,\n313\t      \"ensemble_fpr_2of3\": 0.11,\n314\t      \"ensemble_fpr_weighted\": 0.09,\n315\t      \"dif_standalone_auroc\": 0.54,\n316\t      \"constat_standalone_auroc\": 0.51,\n317\t      \"dvd_standalone_auroc\": 0.47,\n318\t      \"ensemble_improvement_over_best_single\": 0.08,\n319\t      \"cross_val_weight_stability\": 0.43,\n320\t      \"fpr_below_010_pct_configs\": 0.45\n321\t    },\n322\t    \"tables\": [\n323\t      {\n324\t        \"name\": \"Table: Ensemble vs Individual Detectors\",\n325\t        \"columns\": [\n326\t          \"method\",\n327\t          \"auroc\",\n328\t          \"fpr\",\n329\t          \"n_models_available\"\n330\t        ],\n331\t        \"rows\": [\n332\t          [\n333\t            \"DIF (MH)\",\n334\t            0.54,\n335\t            0.31,\n336\t            5227\n337\t          ],\n338\t          [\n339\t            \"ConStat\",\n340\t            0.51,\n341\t            0.06,\n342\t            15\n343\t          ],\n344\t          [\n345\t            \"DVD\",\n346\t            0.47,\n347\t            0.09,\n348\t            12\n349\t          ],\n350\t          [\n351\t            \"2-of-3 majority\",\n352\t            0.58,\n353\t            0.11,\n354\t            12\n355\t          ],\n356\t          [\n357\t            \"weighted fusion\",\n358\t            0.62,\n359\t            0.09,\n360\t            12\n361\t          ]\n362\t        ]\n363\t      }\n364\t    ],\n365\t    \"figures\": [],\n366\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_003c 被 drop 是正确决策。Ensemble 面临三重困难： (a) ground truth circularity, (b) small-N signal components, (c) marginal improvement。 Paper framing 已正确将 ensemble 移至 \\\"future work\\\"。 在 rebuttal 中，如果评审问 \\\"why not ensemble?\\\"，回答是 \\\"ensemble requires validated ground truth, which our Claim 2 shows doesn't exist; building the ground truth infrastructure (Claim 3) is prerequisite\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：ensemble 无法达到预期目标。 1) FPR<0.10 只在 45% 的配置下成立——不满足 \\\"across all configurations\\\" 的目标。 Weighted fusion FPR=0.09 勉强达标，但 cross-val weight stability=0.43 说明 weights 在 folds 之间不稳定，overfitting risk 高。 2) AUROC 提升 +0.08 over best single signal——marginal，且受限于 ground truth 的质量（Li et al. labels 作为 ground truth 本身是 plan 质疑的对象）。 3) 根本矛盾：paper 的 Claim 2 论证 web-overlap labels 不适合评估 item-level detectors，然后用这些 labels 训练 ensemble weights。评审会指出 circularity。 4) 003a/003b 的小样本 (N=12-15 models) 使得 ensemble 的 training data 极有限。 Median 档评审：\\\"the ensemble adds complexity without resolving the fundamental ground truth problem the paper itself identifies\\\"。\\n\"\n367\t  },\n368\t  {\n369\t    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n370\t    \"description\": \"GSM8K 上复制 DIF 分析，GSM1K 作为 contamination ground truth。三步： temporal DIF → semi-synthetic → GSM1K correlation。\\n\",\n371\t    \"results\": {\n372\t      \"step1_gsm8k_n_items\": 1319,\n373\t      \"step1_n_ref\": 1017,\n374\t      \"step1_n_foc\": 804,\n375\t      \"step1_standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n376\t      \"step1_external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n377\t      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n378\t      \"step1_standard_external_spearman\": 0.926,\n379\t      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n380\t      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n381\t      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n382\t      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n383\t      \"step3_pearson_p\": 0.005,\n384\t      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n385\t      \"step3_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n386\t      \"step3_partial_r\": -0.385,\n387\t      \"step3_partial_p\": 0.027,\n388\t      \"step3_bca_ci_pearson\": [\n389\t        -0.714,\n390\t        -0.155\n391\t      ],\n392\t      \"step3_bca_ci_spearman\": [\n393\t        -0.687,\n394\t        -0.031\n395\t      ],\n396\t      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014\n397\t    },\n398\t    \"tables\": [\n399\t      {\n400\t        \"name\": \"Table: GSM8K Temporal DIF Summary\",\n401\t        \"columns\": [\n402\t          \"matching\",\n403\t          \"c_pct\",\n404\t          \"sanity_c_pct\",\n405\t          \"delta_tpr_p10\"\n406\t        ],\n407\t        \"rows\": [\n408\t          [\n409\t            \"standard (total score)\",\n410\t            18.9,\n411\t            0.3,\n412\t            0.818\n413\t          ],\n414\t          [\n415\t            \"external (MMLU score)\",\n416\t            47.4,\n417\t            \"—\",\n418\t            0.517\n419\t          ]\n420\t        ]\n421\t      },\n422\t      {\n423\t        \"name\": \"Table: GSM1K Correlation (Step 3) — Reviewer Critique Points\",\n424\t        \"columns\": [\n425\t          \"statistic\",\n426\t          \"value\",\n427\t          \"95% CI\",\n428\t          \"reviewer_concern\"\n429\t        ],\n430\t        \"rows\": [\n431\t          [\n432\t            \"Pearson r\",\n433\t            -0.478,\n434\t            \"[-0.714, -0.155]\",\n435\t            \"CI wide\"\n436\t          ],\n437\t          [\n438\t            \"Spearman ρ\",\n439\t            -0.403,\n440\t            \"[-0.687, -0.031]\",\n441\t            \"upper bound near zero\"\n442\t          ],\n443\t          [\n444\t            \"Partial r\",\n445\t            -0.385,\n446\t            \"[-0.640, -0.058]\",\n447\t            \"controlling accuracy helps marginally\"\n448\t          ],\n449\t          [\n450\t            \"N\",\n451\t            33,\n452\t            \"—\",\n453\t            \"underpowered\"\n454\t          ]\n455\t        ]\n456\t      }\n457\t    ],\n458\t    \"figures\": [],\n459\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_004 是 mixed outcome。Step 1+2 加强 Claim 1+3 的 cross-benchmark generalizability故事，Step 3 是 liability。正确策略是： 主文用 Step 1+2 证明 \\\"DIF and semi-synthetic framework generalize to GSM8K\\\"， Step 3 降级至 appendix with explicit caveat \\\"suggestive evidence requiring replication with larger matched sample (N≥100)\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心动态：Step 1+2 稳固，Step 3 被 dismiss。 1) Step 1: GSM8K C%=18.9% (低于 MMLU 31.3%) 合理——GSM8K 是 math domain， temporal capability gain 更 uniform，所以 differential 更少。评审接受。 2) Step 2: ΔTPR=+0.818 非常强——比 MMLU 的 +0.674 还好，因为 GSM8K 是 single-domain，within-subject/cross-subject 区分不 applicable，matching 更干净。 Semi-synthetic framework portability 得到确认，Claim 3 加分。 3) Step 3: r=-0.478, p=0.005 但 N=33，BCa CI upper bound |r|=0.155。 Median 档下 1-2 个评审直接 dismiss： - \\\"N=33 with Spearman CI touching zero (−0.031) — underpowered\\\" - \\\"BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155] is too wide to be informative\\\" - \\\"contamination gap is itself a noisy proxy\\\" 方向正确 (negative correlation = DIF items resist contamination gains) 但 统计力不足以成为 independent evidence。 4) 策略：median 档下 Step 3 从 Claim 4 子发现降级至 appendix \\\"suggestive evidence\\\"， Claim 4 主要靠 plan_017 z-score + plan_020 circularity ablation。\\n\"\n460\t  },\n461\t  {\n462\t    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n463\t    \"description\": \"在 MMLU 上拟合 bifactor IRT 模型 (general + 57 subject-specific factors)， 选择 anchor items，执行 fixed-parameter calibration 的 equating pilot。\\n\",\n464\t    \"results\": {\n465\t      \"bifactor_convergence\": true,\n466\t      \"bifactor_iterations\": 2847,\n467\t      \"rmsea\": 0.052,\n468\t      \"cfi\": 0.81,\n469\t      \"tli\": 0.78,\n470\t      \"srmr\": 0.068,\n471\t      \"general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.34,\n472\t      \"subject_factors_variance_explained\": 0.41,\n473\t      \"residual_variance\": 0.25,\n474\t      \"n_anchor_items_selected\": 1200,\n475\t      \"anchor_selection_criterion\": \"no DIF + discrimination > 0.5 + fit residual < 2.0\",\n476\t      \"equated_rho_vs_original\": 0.94,\n477\t      \"equated_rho_target\": 0.95,\n478\t      \"target_met\": false,\n479\t      \"computation_time_hours\": 38,\n480\t      \"memory_peak_gb\": 127\n481\t    },\n482\t    \"tables\": [\n483\t      {\n484\t        \"name\": \"Table: Bifactor IRT Fit Indices\",\n485\t        \"columns\": [\n486\t          \"index\",\n487\t          \"value\",\n488\t          \"conventional_threshold\",\n489\t          \"interpretation\"\n490\t        ],\n491\t        \"rows\": [\n492\t          [\n493\t            \"RMSEA\",\n494\t            0.052,\n495\t            \"<0.06 acceptable\",\n496\t            \"borderline acceptable\"\n497\t          ],\n498\t          [\n499\t            \"CFI\",\n500\t            0.81,\n501\t            \">0.90 good\",\n502\t            \"below threshold\"\n503\t          ],\n504\t          [\n505\t            \"TLI\",\n506\t            0.78,\n507\t            \">0.90 good\",\n508\t            \"below threshold\"\n509\t          ],\n510\t          [\n511\t            \"SRMR\",\n512\t            0.068,\n513\t            \"<0.08 acceptable\",\n514\t            \"acceptable\"\n515\t          ],\n516\t          [\n517\t            \"general factor % variance\",\n518\t            \"34%\",\n519\t            \">50% for unidimensional\",\n520\t            \"confirms multidimensionality\"\n521\t          ]\n522\t        ]\n523\t      }\n524\t    ],\n525\t    \"figures\": [],\n526\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_005 验证了 IRT misspecification 但未解决它。 34% general factor variance 是回应 \\\"IRT misspecification\\\" concern 的有力数据—— 证明 1D IRT 确实不足，但 DIF finding 的方向和规模不受根本影响 (因为 bifactor 校正后 C% 从 31.3% 只降至 ~28-29%，仍然 substantial)。 关键洞察：评审要求的不是 \\\"fix the misspecification\\\"，而是 \\\"show DIF findings are robust TO the misspecification\\\"。Plan_005 可以回答这个——如果 bifactor 校正后 DIF 发现 qualitatively 不变，那就是 robustness evidence。 策略：不把 equating 当 claim，而是作为 IRT sensitivity analysis 放 appendix。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：bifactor 收敛但 fit 指标 mediocre。 1) RMSEA=0.052 在 acceptable range (< 0.06) 但不 good (< 0.05)。 CFI=0.81 和 TLI=0.78 低于常规 threshold (0.90)——这是 12,508 items × 5,227 models 的规模效应，absolute fit indices 在超大规模下系统偏低。 评审如果懂 psychometrics 会接受，不懂会直接攻击 \\\"poor model fit\\\"。 2) General factor 只解释 34% variance——MMLU 的 57 subject 确实 highly multidimensional，这 validates \\\"1D IRT is misspecified\\\" 的论点。 3) Equating ρ=0.94 未达 0.95 target——marginal miss。Plan_014 within-subject pre-check (38.1% C%) 已经预示 DIF 在 bifactor 校正后不会大幅下降。 4) 计算成本高 (38 hours, 127GB RAM)——scalability concern。 Median 档评审反应： - 支持者：\\\"bifactor results validate the multidimensionality concern and motivate\\n  future work on MIRT-based DIF\\\"\\n- 反对者：\\\"CFI=0.81 means the model doesn't fit, equating results are unreliable\\\" 总体：pilot 结果 suggestive 但不 conclusive，适合 limitations/future work。\\n\"\n527\t  },\n528\t  {\n529\t    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n530\t    \"description\": \"为 DIF-flagged items 生成替代题目，用 student simulation 校准难度。\\n\",\n531\t    \"results\": {\n532\t      \"n_items_generated\": 150,\n533\t      \"difficulty_correlation_prompt_based\": 0.32,\n534\t      \"difficulty_correlation_student_sim\": 0.58,\n535\t      \"difficulty_correlation_target\": 0.75,\n536\t      \"target_met\": false,\n537\t      \"cognitive_level_match_rate\": 0.71,\n538\t      \"subject_match_rate\": 0.95,\n539\t      \"human_quality_rating\": 3.2,\n540\t      \"human_quality_scale\": \"1-5\",\n541\t      \"holdout_panel_rho\": 0.52,\n542\t      \"gpu_hours_used\": 145\n543\t    },\n544\t    \"tables\": [\n545\t      {\n546\t        \"name\": \"Table: Item Generation Difficulty Calibration\",\n547\t        \"columns\": [\n548\t          \"method\",\n549\t          \"difficulty_ρ\",\n550\t          \"n_items\",\n551\t          \"notes\"\n552\t        ],\n553\t        \"rows\": [\n554\t          [\n555\t            \"prompt-based targeting\",\n556\t            0.32,\n557\t            150,\n558\t            \"below literature 0.10-0.45\"\n559\t          ],\n560\t          [\n561\t            \"student simulation\",\n562\t            0.58,\n563\t            150,\n564\t            \"below target 0.75\"\n565\t          ],\n566\t          [\n567\t            \"combined (iterative)\",\n568\t            0.61,\n569\t            80,\n570\t            \"2-round refinement\"\n571\t          ]\n572\t        ]\n573\t      }\n574\t    ],\n575\t    \"figures\": [],\n576\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_006 是 expected negative。Item generation 是 hard open problem， failure 不损害核心 paper 因为 regeneration 已从 claims 中 drop。 唯一价值：作为 future work 动机——\\\"automated benchmark maintenance requires better item generation, which remains an open problem\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：item generation 是 paper 最弱的环节之一。 1) Prompt-based difficulty targeting ρ=0.32 远低于文献报告的 0.45 upper bound—— MMLU 的 multiple-choice 格式和 domain diversity 使 prompt 控制困难。 2) Student simulation 提升到 ρ=0.58 (vs 文献 0.75-0.82 on simpler benchmarks)—— MMLU 的 57 domains 使 simulation calibration 更难泛化。 3) Cognitive level match rate 71%——约 29% 的 generated items 测量不同的 cognitive level，这是 construct validity threat。 4) Holdout panel ρ=0.52——远低于 equating 需要的精度。 Median 档评审会直接判定 item generation 不成熟：\\\"generated items don't match target difficulty well enough for equating; this is a negative result\\\"。 策略：plan_006 在 median 档是 negative result，移至 appendix 作为 \\\"current limitations of LLM-based item generation for benchmark maintenance\\\"。 不影响核心 claims。\\n\"\n577\t  },\n578\t  {\n579\t    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n580\t    \"description\": \"实现 Sinharay et al. (2006) 的 cumulative Bayesian DIF prior。 模拟 4 次 successive benchmark administration，展示 evidence 累积带来的 power 提升。\\n\",\n581\t    \"results\": {\n582\t      \"simulation_n_administrations\": 4,\n583\t      \"admin_1_power_delta10\": 0.41,\n584\t      \"admin_2_power_delta10\": 0.56,\n585\t      \"admin_3_power_delta10\": 0.68,\n586\t      \"admin_4_power_delta10\": 0.74,\n587\t      \"target_admin3_power\": 0.7,\n588\t      \"target_met\": false,\n589\t      \"admin_3_power_delta14\": 0.82,\n590\t      \"fpr_cumulative\": 0.048,\n591\t      \"fpr_stable_across_admins\": true,\n592\t      \"bayes_factor_median_admin3\": 4.2,\n593\t      \"simulation_n_items\": 500,\n594\t      \"simulation_n_models_per_admin\": 200,\n595\t      \"computation_time_hours\": 6\n596\t    },\n597\t    \"tables\": [\n598\t      {\n599\t        \"name\": \"Table: Cumulative Power by Administration\",\n600\t        \"columns\": [\n601\t          \"n_admins\",\n602\t          \"power_delta_10\",\n603\t          \"power_delta_14\",\n604\t          \"power_delta_16\",\n605\t          \"fpr\"\n606\t        ],\n607\t        \"rows\": [\n608\t          [\n609\t            1,\n610\t            0.41,\n611\t            0.68,\n612\t            0.72,\n613\t            0.042\n614\t          ],\n615\t          [\n616\t            2,\n617\t            0.56,\n618\t            0.77,\n619\t            0.83,\n620\t            0.045\n621\t          ],\n622\t          [\n623\t            3,\n624\t            0.68,\n625\t            0.82,\n626\t            0.89,\n627\t            0.048\n628\t          ],\n629\t          [\n630\t            4,\n631\t            0.74,\n632\t            0.86,\n633\t            0.92,\n634\t            0.047\n635\t          ]\n636\t        ]\n637\t      }\n638\t    ],\n639\t    \"figures\": [],\n640\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_007 有 modest value 作为 forward-looking contribution。 核心问题：ML 评审对 \\\"future benchmark administrations\\\" 的 temporal framing 不熟悉——psychometrics 中 repeated test administration 是常态， 但 LLM benchmarks 通常是 one-shot。需要明确解释 \\\"as new model generations emerge, the same benchmark is effectively re-administered\\\"。 Appendix 放置，主文 limitations 中一句话提及 cumulative power improvement 可能性。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：simulation 结果方向正确但 target 未达。 1) 3 次 administration 后 δ=1.0 的 power 从 0.41 升至 0.68——接近但未达 0.70 target。 δ=1.4 时 0.82 是可用的，说明 cumulative approach 有价值但主要对 medium effects。 2) FPR 控制良好 (0.048)，Bayesian prior 没有引入 FPR inflation。 3) 核心限制：这是 pure simulation，没有 real data validation。 METABENCH 只有一个 \\\"administration\\\"（没有 temporal sub-cohorts fine enough for 4 successive periods）。 4) Median 档评审：\\\"simulation-only result without empirical validation; interesting but speculative\\\"。 策略：appendix material。展示 concept 可行性但承认需要真实数据验证。 如果 ICLR 评审不熟悉 Bayesian DIF，这部分可能被完全忽略。\\n\"\n641\t  },\n642\t  {\n643\t    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n644\t    \"description\": \"分析 benchmark validity 在 progressive item replacement 下的退化模式。\\n\",\n645\t    \"results\": {\n646\t      \"replacement_5pct_rho\": 0.998,\n647\t      \"replacement_10pct_rho\": 0.995,\n648\t      \"replacement_20pct_rho\": 0.987,\n649\t      \"replacement_50pct_rho\": 0.961,\n650\t      \"reliability_5pct_alpha\": 0.943,\n651\t      \"reliability_10pct_alpha\": 0.938,\n652\t      \"reliability_20pct_alpha\": 0.924,\n653\t      \"reliability_50pct_alpha\": 0.891,\n654\t      \"original_alpha\": 0.946,\n655\t      \"construct_coverage_20pct_subjects_lost\": 0,\n656\t      \"construct_coverage_50pct_subjects_lost\": 3,\n657\t      \"validity_floor_replacement_pct\": 0.35,\n658\t      \"validity_floor_criterion\": \"ρ > 0.98 AND α > 0.92\"\n659\t    },\n660\t    \"tables\": [\n661\t      {\n662\t        \"name\": \"Table: Validity Metrics Under Progressive Replacement\",\n663\t        \"columns\": [\n664\t          \"replacement_pct\",\n665\t          \"rank_ρ\",\n666\t          \"cronbach_α\",\n667\t          \"subjects_under_represented\"\n668\t        ],\n669\t        \"rows\": [\n670\t          [\n671\t            0,\n672\t            1.0,\n673\t            0.946,\n674\t            0\n675\t          ],\n676\t          [\n677\t            5,\n678\t            0.998,\n679\t            0.943,\n680\t            0\n681\t          ],\n682\t          [\n683\t            10,\n684\t            0.995,\n685\t            0.938,\n686\t            0\n687\t          ],\n688\t          [\n689\t            20,\n690\t            0.987,\n691\t            0.924,\n692\t            0\n693\t          ],\n694\t          [\n695\t            35,\n696\t            0.974,\n697\t            0.908,\n698\t            1\n699\t          ],\n700\t          [\n701\t            50,\n702\t            0.961,\n703\t            0.891,\n704\t            3\n705\t          ]\n706\t        ]\n707\t      }\n708\t    ],\n709\t    \"figures\": [],\n710\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_008 的主要贡献是量化 \\\"how much replacement is safe\\\"—— 35% validity floor 直接对应 \\\"31% DIF items can be safely replaced without validity loss\\\"。这 strengthens the \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative。 但 plan_006 的 negative result 使得 \\\"replacement\\\" 变成 theoretical exercise。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：graceful degradation 结果 clean 且 informative。 1) ρ 从 0.998 (5%) 到 0.961 (50%) 的退化曲线非常 smooth——MMLU 的 12,508 items 有 massive redundancy，即使替换 50% items 排名仍 strongly correlated。 这 complements plan_017 (ρ=0.997 after removing 31% DIF items)。 2) Reliability (Cronbach's α) 从 0.946 到 0.891——20% 是 practical threshold， 之后 reliability 下降加速。 3) Construct coverage：50% replacement 时 3 个 subjects 可能 under-represented (small subjects with few items)。 4) 核心问题：replacement 假设 generated items 质量 OK——但 plan_006 显示 generation 质量不足。所以 \\\"graceful degradation\\\" 只在理论层面成立。 Median 档评审：\\\"nice analysis but moot without better item generation (plan_006 failed)\\\"。 策略：clean supplementary result，放 appendix。主文用 \\\"validity floor at ~35% replacement\\\" 作为 practical recommendation。\\n\"\n711\t  },\n712\t  {\n713\t    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n714\t    \"description\": \"Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees 作为 categorical DIF 的替代方案。 Treat model release date as continuous covariate。\\n\",\n715\t    \"results\": {\n716\t      \"n_items_analyzed\": 12508,\n717\t      \"n_items_with_significant_split\": 4127,\n718\t      \"pct_items_with_split\": 33.0,\n719\t      \"primary_split_date\": \"2023-11-15\",\n720\t      \"concordance_with_mh_ets_c\": 0.78,\n721\t      \"additional_items_detected\": 209,\n722\t      \"items_missed_by_ift\": 612,\n723\t      \"jaccard_mh_vs_ift\": 0.68,\n724\t      \"computational_time_hours\": 12,\n725\t      \"n_items_nonlinear_trend\": 1834,\n726\t      \"pct_nonlinear\": 14.7\n727\t    },\n728\t    \"tables\": [\n729\t      {\n730\t        \"name\": \"Table: MH vs IFT Concordance\",\n731\t        \"columns\": [\n732\t          \"metric\",\n733\t          \"mh_ets_c\",\n734\t          \"ift_significant\",\n735\t          \"overlap\",\n736\t          \"jaccard\"\n737\t        ],\n738\t        \"rows\": [\n739\t          [\n740\t            \"n_flagged\",\n741\t            3918,\n742\t            4127,\n743\t            3306,\n744\t            0.68\n745\t          ],\n746\t          [\n747\t            \"pct_flagged\",\n748\t            31.3,\n749\t            33.0,\n750\t            26.4,\n751\t            \"—\"\n752\t          ]\n753\t        ]\n754\t      }\n755\t    ],\n756\t    \"figures\": [],\n757\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_009 的 concordance=0.78 有两面性： - 支持：MH 的 categorical split 不是 artifact，IFT confirms temporal instability - 质疑：22% discordance 说明 method choice matters，results are partially method-dependent 评审在 median 档接受 IFT 作为 robustness check，不会深入追究 discordance。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：IFT 是有价值的 robustness check 但不改变 narrative。 1) 33% items with significant split vs MH 31.3%——high concordance (0.78)， 说明 categorical temporal split 不是 arbitrary 的。 2) Primary split date 2023-11-15——接近 GPT-4/Llama-2 到 Llama-3/Mixtral 的代际转换点，有 face validity。 3) IFT detects 209 additional items that MH misses (mostly items with gradual drift rather than sharp shift)，同时 misses 612 items MH catches (mostly items where DIF is large but not monotone in date)。 4) 14.7% nonlinear trends——说明 some items 的 DIF 不是 monotone temporal， 暗示 \\\"contamination + capability gain + item drift\\\" 的 multi-factor story。 Median 档评审：\\\"useful supplementary analysis, confirms MH results are not artifacts of the cohort split\\\"。不改变 claims 但提供 methodological robustness。 策略：appendix 的 robustness check。主文一句话：\\\"IFT with continuous release date yields 78% concordance with MH categorical DIF (Appendix X)\\\"。\\n\"\n758\t  },\n759\t  {\n760\t    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n761\t    \"description\": \"在 decoder-only 子群内重跑 DIF，检验 architecture heterogeneity 是否影响 IRT fit。\\n\",\n762\t    \"results\": {\n763\t      \"n_decoder_only\": 5226,\n764\t      \"n_non_decoder\": 1,\n765\t      \"pct_decoder_only\": 99.98,\n766\t      \"decoder_only_c_pct\": 31.3,\n767\t      \"full_population_c_pct\": 31.3,\n768\t      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n769\t      \"irt_rmsea_full\": 0.089,\n770\t      \"irt_rmsea_decoder_only\": 0.088,\n771\t      \"irt_cfi_full\": 0.72,\n772\t      \"irt_cfi_decoder_only\": 0.72,\n773\t      \"irt_fit_improvement\": \"negligible\",\n774\t      \"pct_models_lz_gt2\": 98.0\n775\t    },\n776\t    \"tables\": [\n777\t      {\n778\t        \"name\": \"Table: Architecture Stratification Results\",\n779\t        \"columns\": [\n780\t          \"population\",\n781\t          \"n_models\",\n782\t          \"c_pct\",\n783\t          \"rmsea\",\n784\t          \"cfi\",\n785\t          \"pct_lz_gt2\"\n786\t        ],\n787\t        \"rows\": [\n788\t          [\n789\t            \"full\",\n790\t            5227,\n791\t            31.3,\n792\t            0.089,\n793\t            0.72,\n794\t            98.0\n795\t          ],\n796\t          [\n797\t            \"decoder-only\",\n798\t            5226,\n799\t            31.3,\n800\t            0.088,\n801\t            0.72,\n802\t            98.0\n803\t          ],\n804\t          [\n805\t            \"delta\",\n806\t            \"—\",\n807\t            0.0,\n808\t            0.001,\n809\t            0.0,\n810\t            0.0\n811\t          ]\n812\t        ]\n813\t      }\n814\t    ],\n815\t    \"figures\": [],\n816\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_010 的 value 是 defensive：排除一个 potential confound。 但它也暴露了真正的问题——IRT misfit 来自 multidimensionality， 这正是评审的 attack vector。Plan_005 bifactor pilot 是 partial response， 但 median 档下不够 convincing (CFI=0.81)。 最佳回应策略：承认 misspecification，展示 DIF 发现在 bifactor 校正后 qualitatively 不变 (C% ~28-29% vs 31.3%)，argue \\\"our findings are conservative estimates\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：plan_010 是 clean knockout result。 1) METABENCH MMLU 是 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227)——removing 1 non-decoder model changes literally nothing (Jaccard=1.0)。 2) IRT fit 不改善 (RMSEA 0.089→0.088, CFI 0.72→0.72)——因为 misfit 来自 MMLU 的 57-subject multidimensionality，不是 architecture heterogeneity。 3) 98% models 有 |Lz|>2——这反映 1D IRT 对 MMLU 的 fundamental misspecification， 不是 population heterogeneity。 Median 档评审接受这个 null result：architecture 不是问题。但会转向 \\\"OK so the misfit is from multidimensionality, have you tried multidimensional IRT?\\\"—— 这是 median 档的核心 concern 之一。 策略：主文用一段报告 99.98% decoder-only + Jaccard=1.0。 IRT fit 数据放 limitations 讨论，作为 multidimensional IRT future work 的动机。\\n\"\n817\t  },\n818\t  {\n819\t    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n820\t    \"description\": \"向真实 METABENCH response matrix 注入已知 contamination，测量 DIF 检测力。\\n\",\n821\t    \"results\": {\n822\t      \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n823\t      \"n_injected_items\": 200,\n824\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n825\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n826\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n827\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n828\t      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n829\t      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n830\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n831\t      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n832\t      \"ability_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302,\n833\t      \"cross_subject_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n834\t      \"within_subject_fpr_inflation_p10\": 0.186,\n835\t      \"dose_response_monotone\": true,\n836\t      \"dose_response_p_values\": [\n837\t        0.3,\n838\t        0.5,\n839\t        0.7,\n840\t        1.0\n841\t      ]\n842\t    },\n843\t    \"tables\": [\n844\t      {\n845\t        \"name\": \"Table: Semi-synthetic Detection Power (Cross-subject Matching)\",\n846\t        \"columns\": [\n847\t          \"exploitation_rate_p\",\n848\t          \"baseline_tpr\",\n849\t          \"injected_tpr\",\n850\t          \"delta_tpr\",\n851\t          \"fpr\",\n852\t          \"delta_fpr\"\n853\t        ],\n854\t        \"rows\": [\n855\t          [\n856\t            \"0.0 (no injection)\",\n857\t            0.326,\n858\t            0.326,\n859\t            0.0,\n860\t            0.314,\n861\t            0.0\n862\t          ],\n863\t          [\n864\t            0.3,\n865\t            0.326,\n866\t            0.548,\n867\t            0.222,\n868\t            0.314,\n869\t            0.0\n870\t          ],\n871\t          [\n872\t            0.5,\n873\t            0.326,\n874\t            0.834,\n875\t            0.508,\n876\t            0.314,\n877\t            0.0\n878\t          ],\n879\t          [\n880\t            0.7,\n881\t            0.326,\n882\t            0.99,\n883\t            0.664,\n884\t            0.314,\n885\t            0.0\n886\t          ],\n887\t          [\n888\t            1.0,\n889\t            0.326,\n890\t            1.0,\n891\t            0.674,\n892\t            0.314,\n893\t            0.0\n894\t          ]\n895\t        ]\n896\t      },\n897\t      {\n898\t        \"name\": \"Table: Within-subject vs Cross-subject Matching\",\n899\t        \"columns\": [\n900\t          \"matching\",\n901\t          \"delta_tpr_p05\",\n902\t          \"delta_fpr_p10\",\n903\t          \"fpr_stable\"\n904\t        ],\n905\t        \"rows\": [\n906\t          [\n907\t            \"within-subject\",\n908\t            0.457,\n909\t            0.186,\n910\t            false\n911\t          ],\n912\t          [\n913\t            \"cross-subject\",\n914\t            0.508,\n915\t            0.0,\n916\t            true\n917\t          ]\n918\t        ]\n919\t      }\n920\t    ],\n921\t    \"figures\": [],\n922\t    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_011 (+plan_016 cross-subject replication) 是 Claim 3 的 robust foundation。Reviewers 在 median 档给 semi-synthetic framework positive marks (novelty sub-score 2.5 on this specific contribution)。 唯一 downside：injection simplicity。Rebuttal 准备： \\\"Our injection flips incorrect→correct, which is the minimal model of contamination (memorized answer). More complex patterns (partial memorization, verbatim recall) would produce LARGER DIF effects, not smaller—our power estimates are conservative.\\\"\\n\\nMedian 档：plan_011 是 paper 的 strongest evidence 之一。 1) ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 是 clean, large effect——从 baseline 0.326 升至 0.834， 明确证明 DIF 能 detect injected differential contamination。 2) Dose-response 从 p=0.3 到 p=1.0 monotone——mechanistic validation。 3) Cross-subject matching ΔFPR=0.000 是 key innovation——完全消除 FPR inflation， vs within-subject matching +0.186。这是 Claim 3 的核心证据。 4) Baseline FPR=0.314 (= temporal C%=31.3%)——评审会问 \\\"is 31% baseline FPR acceptable?\\\" Answer: this IS the real DIF rate, not false positives. Semi-synthetic 只 adds signal on top of real baseline。 Median 档评审对 plan_011 的质疑集中在： - \\\"injection mechanism (incorrect→correct) is simplistic—real contamination\\n  may produce different patterns (e.g., faster response time, different error types)\\\"\\n- \\\"you inject into real matrices, but the contamination is still artificial\\\" 这些是 acknowledged limitations，不是 fatal flaws。 策略：plan_011 在主文 §4 占重要位置。Cross-subject matching 作为 methodological recommendation 明确 highlight。\\n\"\n923\t  }\n924\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c6b9965-4730-46a2-a3a4-07c965d9e09e","uuid":"6cd1033b-ae4b-4e8c-8388-031648f3acfb","timestamp":"2026-05-21T06:44:30.565Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T062008/median/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"real_data_dif_mmlu\",\n    \"description\": \"METABENCH MMLU 全量 DIF 分析。temporal/ability/within-family 三种 cohort 定义， 加 Li et al. proxy validation 和 domain specificity。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"temporal_ets_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"temporal_n_c_items\": 3918,\n      \"temporal_n_total\": 12508,\n      \"temporal_fpr_on_li_clean\": 0.318,\n      \"temporal_enrichment_ratio\": 0.96,\n      \"ability_ets_c_pct\": 2.9,\n      \"ability_enrichment\": 1.19,\n      \"within_family_llama2v3_c_pct\": 61.3,\n      \"within_family_mistral_mixtral_c_pct\": 38.7,\n      \"domain_spearman_rho\": 0.307,\n      \"domain_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"sanity_random_split_c_pct\": 0.18,\n      \"temporal_ability_jaccard\": 0.014\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary by ETS Classification\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"ets_class\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"pct\",\n          \"mean_abs_delta_mh\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"A (negligible)\",\n            8590,\n            68.7,\n            0.43\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B (moderate)\",\n            2641,\n            21.1,\n            1.24\n          ],\n          [\n            \"C (large)\",\n            1277,\n            10.2,\n            2.31\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B+C (flagged)\",\n            3918,\n            31.3,\n            1.58\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Cohort Definition Sensitivity\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"cohort\",\n          \"n_ref\",\n          \"n_foc\",\n          \"c_pct\",\n          \"enrichment\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"temporal (2023 vs 2024-H1)\",\n            1253,\n            656,\n            31.3,\n            0.96\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ability (Q1 vs Q5)\",\n            \"~1044\",\n            \"~1044\",\n            2.9,\n            1.19\n          ],\n          [\n            \"within-family (Llama-2 vs 3)\",\n            161,\n            308,\n            61.3,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"random split (sanity)\",\n            950,\n            950,\n            0.18,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_001 是 paper 的基石。数据本身不受质疑，但 \\\"so what\\\" 需要后续实验 (plan_019, plan_017, plan_020) 支撑。评审预期反应： R1: \\\"Impressive scale, but what does 31% instability mean for practitioners?\\\" R2: \\\"The enrichment≈1.0 result is interesting but undermines the contamination framing\\\" R3: \\\"Within-family results suggest capability gain, not contamination\\\" 总体：plan_001 在 median 档得 strong accept 作为 empirical contribution， 但单独不够——需要 downstream impact story。\\n\\n\\nmedian 档下这些数值本身站得住——31.3% 是 robust 的经验发现，random-split sanity (0.18%) 排除统计伪影， domain ρ=0.307 是 modest ecological correlation。问题不在数字，在解读： 1) enrichment≈1.0 证明 DIF 和 web-overlap labels 正交，但评审会问 \\\"if DIF doesn't correlate with known contamination, what IS it detecting?\\\"——需要 plan_019 decomposition 才能回答 \\\"item-specific instability, not capability gain\\\"。 2) within-family C%=61.3% (Llama-2 vs 3) 远高于 cross-cohort 31.3%，评审会质疑 \\\"within-family analysis proves capability gain drives DIF, not contamination\\\"。 Median 档下 1 个评审接受 \\\"capability gain ≠ item instability\\\" 论证，1 个不接受。 3) domain ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 在 median 档被视为 \\\"interesting but not definitive\\\"， 不被攻击也不加分。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_robustness_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"验证 DIF 在 RL-trained 模型上的鲁棒性。SFT baseline vs alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO) vs reasoning-RL (GRPO/PPO)。关键在于 reasoning-RL 只有 10-15 个模型。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_cohort_n\": 312,\n      \"alignment_rl_cohort_n\": 477,\n      \"reasoning_rl_models_collected\": 13,\n      \"sft_vs_alignment_jaccard_dif_flags\": 0.72,\n      \"sft_temporal_c_pct\": 30.8,\n      \"alignment_rl_temporal_c_pct\": 32.1,\n      \"combined_with_reasoning_rl_c_pct\": 31.5,\n      \"jaccard_base_vs_rl_augmented\": 0.91,\n      \"tost_equivalence_p\": 0.14,\n      \"tost_equivalence_bound\": 0.05,\n      \"tost_verdict\": \"inconclusive\",\n      \"mink_auroc_sft\": 0.61,\n      \"mink_auroc_alignment_rl\": 0.58,\n      \"mink_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.43,\n      \"constat_auroc_sft\": 0.64,\n      \"constat_auroc_reasoning_rl\": 0.39,\n      \"delong_p_mink_sft_vs_rl\": 0.08,\n      \"delong_p_constat_sft_vs_rl\": 0.03,\n      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_diff_mink\": [\n        -0.02,\n        0.38\n      ],\n      \"bootstrap_ci_auroc_diff_constat\": [\n        0.04,\n        0.46\n      ],\n      \"power_analysis_delta_boundary\": 1.1,\n      \"power_analysis_tpr_at_boundary\": 0.42\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: DIF Flag Stability Under Cohort Composition Change\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"cohort_composition\",\n          \"n_total\",\n          \"c_pct\",\n          \"jaccard_vs_baseline\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"SFT only\",\n            312,\n            30.8,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SFT + alignment-RL\",\n            789,\n            32.1,\n            0.72\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SFT + alignment-RL + reasoning-RL\",\n            802,\n            31.5,\n            0.91\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Individual Detector AUROC by Model Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"detector\",\n          \"sft\",\n          \"alignment_rl\",\n          \"reasoning_rl\",\n          \"delong_p\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Min-K%\",\n            0.61,\n            0.58,\n            0.43,\n            0.08\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            0.64,\n            0.6,\n            0.39,\n            0.03\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DIF (group)\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"N/A\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_002 是最弱的实验。N=13 reasoning-RL 无法支撑任何统计结论。 TOST inconclusive 意味着既不能声称 robust 也不能声称 fragile。 最佳策略：power analysis 图放 appendix，主文用一句话承认 \\\"reasoning-RL validation remains underpowered (N=13); alignment-RL cohort (N=477) shows stable DIF flags (Jaccard=0.72 vs SFT)\\\"。不把 RL robustness 作为 claim。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心问题：N=13 reasoning-RL 模型严重不足。 1) Group-level DIF flags 在加入 13 个 RL 模型后变化很小 (Jaccard=0.91)，因为 N=13 在 N≈1900 focal cohort 中占比 <1%，统计上几乎无影响。评审会正确指出 \\\"this doesn't prove RL robustness, it proves RL models are too few to matter\\\"。 2) TOST 等价性检验 p=0.14 不显著——无法证明等价，也无法证明差异。 Median 档评审判断：inconclusive，移至 limitations。 3) 个体模型检测：ConStat 在 reasoning-RL 上 AUROC 降至 0.39 (显著下降)， 但 DIF 是 group-level 无法做个体比较，comparison 不对等。 4) Power analysis 有理论价值：δ<1.1 时 TPR<0.42，清晰刻画了 detection boundary。 但评审会说 \\\"you characterized a limitation, not solved it\\\"。 总体：plan_002 在 median 档被降级为 appendix，N=13 是 fatal underpowering。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"constat_perturbation_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"独立评估 ConStat-style perturbation testing 在 MMLU 上的检测力。 200+ items paraphrased，comparison with DIF flags。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_paraphrased\": 217,\n      \"paraphrase_quality_human_eval\": 0.78,\n      \"constat_detection_rate_fdr005\": 0.23,\n      \"constat_detection_rate_fdr010\": 0.31,\n      \"constat_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.08,\n      \"constat_fpr_on_clean_items\": 0.06,\n      \"constat_effect_size_non_rl\": 0.74,\n      \"constat_effect_size_rl\": 0.31,\n      \"paraphrase_difficulty_shift_mean\": 0.12,\n      \"paraphrase_difficulty_shift_std\": 0.34,\n      \"n_models_tested\": 15,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 62\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: ConStat Detection Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"non_rl_models\",\n          \"rl_models\",\n          \"all\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"n_models\",\n            11,\n            4,\n            15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"detection_rate_fdr005\",\n            0.27,\n            0.14,\n            0.23\n          ],\n          [\n            \"mean_effect_size\",\n            0.74,\n            0.31,\n            0.61\n          ],\n          [\n            \"FPR\",\n            0.05,\n            0.08,\n            0.06\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_003a 提供了有价值的 baseline comparison，但不构成独立贡献。 ConStat-DIF orthogonality (Jaccard=0.08) 支持 meta-critique (不同方法 capture 不同 aspects)，但 N=15 模型限制了结论强度。适合 appendix 作为 related work empirical comparison，不适合 main body。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：ConStat 实验执行了但结果 mixed。 1) Paraphrase 质量 78% human-eval acceptable——约 22% 的 reformulation 引入了 subtle semantic shift，导致 difficulty 变化不纯粹来自 contamination。 评审会质疑 paraphrase 质量是 confound。 2) FDR-controlled detection rate 23% 在 non-RL 模型上——reasonable baseline 但 不 impressive。Jaccard=0.08 与 DIF 几乎无 overlap，说明两者 detect 不同 signal。 3) RL 模型上 effect size 从 0.74 降至 0.31——方向正确但 N=15 模型下 CI 非常宽。 4) 核心问题：ConStat 需要 inference access (running paraphrased items through models)， 而 METABENCH 只有 original responses。所以 ConStat 只在 15 个有 inference access 的模型上跑，vs DIF 用全部 5,227 模型。Scale 不可比。 Median 档评审判断：\\\"useful baseline comparison but limited by small inference sample\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\",\n    \"description\": \"DVD generation variance 在 MMLU 上的独立评估。50 responses/item via temperature sampling。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_models_tested\": 12,\n      \"n_items_tested\": 500,\n      \"responses_per_item\": 50,\n      \"temperature\": 0.8,\n      \"bimodal_detection_rate\": 0.14,\n      \"bimodal_verbatim_contamination\": 0.31,\n      \"bimodal_variant_contamination\": 0.06,\n      \"dvd_dif_overlap_jaccard\": 0.05,\n      \"dvd_fpr\": 0.09,\n      \"variance_score_reliability\": 0.62,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 58\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: DVD Detection by Contamination Type\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"contamination_type\",\n          \"n_items_tested\",\n          \"bimodal_rate\",\n          \"fpr\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"verbatim\",\n            150,\n            0.31,\n            0.08\n          ],\n          [\n            \"variant\",\n            150,\n            0.06,\n            0.1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"clean\",\n            200,\n            \"—\",\n            0.09\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_003b 是最弱的独立实验。Detection power 低于 ConStat， 且需要 open-weight inference access。主要价值是证明 \\\"generation variance alone is insufficient\\\"——但这不是 surprising finding。Appendix material at best。 在 median 档的策略调整中，plan_003b 应被 deprioritized。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：DVD 结果较弱。 1) 只有 14% 的 items 显示 bimodal generation variance——远低于 DIF 的 31.3%， 说明 generation variance 作为 contamination signal 灵敏度较低。 2) Verbatim contamination (31% bimodal) vs variant contamination (6% bimodal)： DVD 几乎只能 detect verbatim memorization，对 variant 无力。 3) 与 DIF 的 overlap 近乎为零 (Jaccard=0.05)，再次说明不同方法 capture 不同 signal。 4) Variance score reliability 0.62——moderate at best。50 responses 可能不足以 稳定估计 variance，但 GPU budget 已耗尽。 5) 核心限制：DVD 需要 open-weight + inference，排除 closed-source models。 Median 档评审：\\\"limited detection power, primarily captures verbatim memorization which is already detectable by simpler methods (n-gram matching)\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ensemble_fusion\",\n    \"description\": \"DIF + ConStat + DVD 三信号 ensemble。依赖 003a 和 003b。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"ensemble_auroc_2of3\": 0.58,\n      \"ensemble_auroc_weighted\": 0.62,\n      \"ensemble_fpr_2of3\": 0.11,\n      \"ensemble_fpr_weighted\": 0.09,\n      \"dif_standalone_auroc\": 0.54,\n      \"constat_standalone_auroc\": 0.51,\n      \"dvd_standalone_auroc\": 0.47,\n      \"ensemble_improvement_over_best_single\": 0.08,\n      \"cross_val_weight_stability\": 0.43,\n      \"fpr_below_010_pct_configs\": 0.45\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Ensemble vs Individual Detectors\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"auroc\",\n          \"fpr\",\n          \"n_models_available\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"DIF (MH)\",\n            0.54,\n            0.31,\n            5227\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ConStat\",\n            0.51,\n            0.06,\n            15\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DVD\",\n            0.47,\n            0.09,\n            12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2-of-3 majority\",\n            0.58,\n            0.11,\n            12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"weighted fusion\",\n            0.62,\n            0.09,\n            12\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_003c 被 drop 是正确决策。Ensemble 面临三重困难： (a) ground truth circularity, (b) small-N signal components, (c) marginal improvement。 Paper framing 已正确将 ensemble 移至 \\\"future work\\\"。 在 rebuttal 中，如果评审问 \\\"why not ensemble?\\\"，回答是 \\\"ensemble requires validated ground truth, which our Claim 2 shows doesn't exist; building the ground truth infrastructure (Claim 3) is prerequisite\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：ensemble 无法达到预期目标。 1) FPR<0.10 只在 45% 的配置下成立——不满足 \\\"across all configurations\\\" 的目标。 Weighted fusion FPR=0.09 勉强达标，但 cross-val weight stability=0.43 说明 weights 在 folds 之间不稳定，overfitting risk 高。 2) AUROC 提升 +0.08 over best single signal——marginal，且受限于 ground truth 的质量（Li et al. labels 作为 ground truth 本身是 plan 质疑的对象）。 3) 根本矛盾：paper 的 Claim 2 论证 web-overlap labels 不适合评估 item-level detectors，然后用这些 labels 训练 ensemble weights。评审会指出 circularity。 4) 003a/003b 的小样本 (N=12-15 models) 使得 ensemble 的 training data 极有限。 Median 档评审：\\\"the ensemble adds complexity without resolving the fundamental ground truth problem the paper itself identifies\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\",\n    \"description\": \"GSM8K 上复制 DIF 分析，GSM1K 作为 contamination ground truth。三步： temporal DIF → semi-synthetic → GSM1K correlation。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"step1_gsm8k_n_items\": 1319,\n      \"step1_n_ref\": 1017,\n      \"step1_n_foc\": 804,\n      \"step1_standard_c_pct\": 18.9,\n      \"step1_external_c_pct\": 47.4,\n      \"step1_sanity_c_pct\": 0.3,\n      \"step1_standard_external_spearman\": 0.926,\n      \"step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.818,\n      \"step2_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.517,\n      \"step3_n_models\": 33,\n      \"step3_pearson_r\": -0.478,\n      \"step3_pearson_p\": 0.005,\n      \"step3_spearman_rho\": -0.403,\n      \"step3_spearman_p\": 0.02,\n      \"step3_partial_r\": -0.385,\n      \"step3_partial_p\": 0.027,\n      \"step3_bca_ci_pearson\": [\n        -0.714,\n        -0.155\n      ],\n      \"step3_bca_ci_spearman\": [\n        -0.687,\n        -0.031\n      ],\n      \"step3_permutation_p\": 0.014\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GSM8K Temporal DIF Summary\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"matching\",\n          \"c_pct\",\n          \"sanity_c_pct\",\n          \"delta_tpr_p10\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"standard (total score)\",\n            18.9,\n            0.3,\n            0.818\n          ],\n          [\n            \"external (MMLU score)\",\n            47.4,\n            \"—\",\n            0.517\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: GSM1K Correlation (Step 3) — Reviewer Critique Points\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"statistic\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"95% CI\",\n          \"reviewer_concern\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Pearson r\",\n            -0.478,\n            \"[-0.714, -0.155]\",\n            \"CI wide\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Spearman ρ\",\n            -0.403,\n            \"[-0.687, -0.031]\",\n            \"upper bound near zero\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Partial r\",\n            -0.385,\n            \"[-0.640, -0.058]\",\n            \"controlling accuracy helps marginally\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"N\",\n            33,\n            \"—\",\n            \"underpowered\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_004 是 mixed outcome。Step 1+2 加强 Claim 1+3 的 cross-benchmark generalizability故事，Step 3 是 liability。正确策略是： 主文用 Step 1+2 证明 \\\"DIF and semi-synthetic framework generalize to GSM8K\\\"， Step 3 降级至 appendix with explicit caveat \\\"suggestive evidence requiring replication with larger matched sample (N≥100)\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档核心动态：Step 1+2 稳固，Step 3 被 dismiss。 1) Step 1: GSM8K C%=18.9% (低于 MMLU 31.3%) 合理——GSM8K 是 math domain， temporal capability gain 更 uniform，所以 differential 更少。评审接受。 2) Step 2: ΔTPR=+0.818 非常强——比 MMLU 的 +0.674 还好，因为 GSM8K 是 single-domain，within-subject/cross-subject 区分不 applicable，matching 更干净。 Semi-synthetic framework portability 得到确认，Claim 3 加分。 3) Step 3: r=-0.478, p=0.005 但 N=33，BCa CI upper bound |r|=0.155。 Median 档下 1-2 个评审直接 dismiss： - \\\"N=33 with Spearman CI touching zero (−0.031) — underpowered\\\" - \\\"BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155] is too wide to be informative\\\" - \\\"contamination gap is itself a noisy proxy\\\" 方向正确 (negative correlation = DIF items resist contamination gains) 但 统计力不足以成为 independent evidence。 4) 策略：median 档下 Step 3 从 Claim 4 子发现降级至 appendix \\\"suggestive evidence\\\"， Claim 4 主要靠 plan_017 z-score + plan_020 circularity ablation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\",\n    \"description\": \"在 MMLU 上拟合 bifactor IRT 模型 (general + 57 subject-specific factors)， 选择 anchor items，执行 fixed-parameter calibration 的 equating pilot。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bifactor_convergence\": true,\n      \"bifactor_iterations\": 2847,\n      \"rmsea\": 0.052,\n      \"cfi\": 0.81,\n      \"tli\": 0.78,\n      \"srmr\": 0.068,\n      \"general_factor_variance_explained\": 0.34,\n      \"subject_factors_variance_explained\": 0.41,\n      \"residual_variance\": 0.25,\n      \"n_anchor_items_selected\": 1200,\n      \"anchor_selection_criterion\": \"no DIF + discrimination > 0.5 + fit residual < 2.0\",\n      \"equated_rho_vs_original\": 0.94,\n      \"equated_rho_target\": 0.95,\n      \"target_met\": false,\n      \"computation_time_hours\": 38,\n      \"memory_peak_gb\": 127\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Bifactor IRT Fit Indices\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"index\",\n          \"value\",\n          \"conventional_threshold\",\n          \"interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RMSEA\",\n            0.052,\n            \"<0.06 acceptable\",\n            \"borderline acceptable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"CFI\",\n            0.81,\n            \">0.90 good\",\n            \"below threshold\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"TLI\",\n            0.78,\n            \">0.90 good\",\n            \"below threshold\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"SRMR\",\n            0.068,\n            \"<0.08 acceptable\",\n            \"acceptable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"general factor % variance\",\n            \"34%\",\n            \">50% for unidimensional\",\n            \"confirms multidimensionality\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_005 验证了 IRT misspecification 但未解决它。 34% general factor variance 是回应 \\\"IRT misspecification\\\" concern 的有力数据—— 证明 1D IRT 确实不足，但 DIF finding 的方向和规模不受根本影响 (因为 bifactor 校正后 C% 从 31.3% 只降至 ~28-29%，仍然 substantial)。 关键洞察：评审要求的不是 \\\"fix the misspecification\\\"，而是 \\\"show DIF findings are robust TO the misspecification\\\"。Plan_005 可以回答这个——如果 bifactor 校正后 DIF 发现 qualitatively 不变，那就是 robustness evidence。 策略：不把 equating 当 claim，而是作为 IRT sensitivity analysis 放 appendix。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：bifactor 收敛但 fit 指标 mediocre。 1) RMSEA=0.052 在 acceptable range (< 0.06) 但不 good (< 0.05)。 CFI=0.81 和 TLI=0.78 低于常规 threshold (0.90)——这是 12,508 items × 5,227 models 的规模效应，absolute fit indices 在超大规模下系统偏低。 评审如果懂 psychometrics 会接受，不懂会直接攻击 \\\"poor model fit\\\"。 2) General factor 只解释 34% variance——MMLU 的 57 subject 确实 highly multidimensional，这 validates \\\"1D IRT is misspecified\\\" 的论点。 3) Equating ρ=0.94 未达 0.95 target——marginal miss。Plan_014 within-subject pre-check (38.1% C%) 已经预示 DIF 在 bifactor 校正后不会大幅下降。 4) 计算成本高 (38 hours, 127GB RAM)——scalability concern。 Median 档评审反应： - 支持者：\\\"bifactor results validate the multidimensionality concern and motivate\\n  future work on MIRT-based DIF\\\"\\n- 反对者：\\\"CFI=0.81 means the model doesn't fit, equating results are unreliable\\\" 总体：pilot 结果 suggestive 但不 conclusive，适合 limitations/future work。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_generation_calibration\",\n    \"description\": \"为 DIF-flagged items 生成替代题目，用 student simulation 校准难度。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_generated\": 150,\n      \"difficulty_correlation_prompt_based\": 0.32,\n      \"difficulty_correlation_student_sim\": 0.58,\n      \"difficulty_correlation_target\": 0.75,\n      \"target_met\": false,\n      \"cognitive_level_match_rate\": 0.71,\n      \"subject_match_rate\": 0.95,\n      \"human_quality_rating\": 3.2,\n      \"human_quality_scale\": \"1-5\",\n      \"holdout_panel_rho\": 0.52,\n      \"gpu_hours_used\": 145\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Item Generation Difficulty Calibration\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"method\",\n          \"difficulty_ρ\",\n          \"n_items\",\n          \"notes\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"prompt-based targeting\",\n            0.32,\n            150,\n            \"below literature 0.10-0.45\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"student simulation\",\n            0.58,\n            150,\n            \"below target 0.75\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"combined (iterative)\",\n            0.61,\n            80,\n            \"2-round refinement\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_006 是 expected negative。Item generation 是 hard open problem， failure 不损害核心 paper 因为 regeneration 已从 claims 中 drop。 唯一价值：作为 future work 动机——\\\"automated benchmark maintenance requires better item generation, which remains an open problem\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：item generation 是 paper 最弱的环节之一。 1) Prompt-based difficulty targeting ρ=0.32 远低于文献报告的 0.45 upper bound—— MMLU 的 multiple-choice 格式和 domain diversity 使 prompt 控制困难。 2) Student simulation 提升到 ρ=0.58 (vs 文献 0.75-0.82 on simpler benchmarks)—— MMLU 的 57 domains 使 simulation calibration 更难泛化。 3) Cognitive level match rate 71%——约 29% 的 generated items 测量不同的 cognitive level，这是 construct validity threat。 4) Holdout panel ρ=0.52——远低于 equating 需要的精度。 Median 档评审会直接判定 item generation 不成熟：\\\"generated items don't match target difficulty well enough for equating; this is a negative result\\\"。 策略：plan_006 在 median 档是 negative result，移至 appendix 作为 \\\"current limitations of LLM-based item generation for benchmark maintenance\\\"。 不影响核心 claims。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"实现 Sinharay et al. (2006) 的 cumulative Bayesian DIF prior。 模拟 4 次 successive benchmark administration，展示 evidence 累积带来的 power 提升。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"simulation_n_administrations\": 4,\n      \"admin_1_power_delta10\": 0.41,\n      \"admin_2_power_delta10\": 0.56,\n      \"admin_3_power_delta10\": 0.68,\n      \"admin_4_power_delta10\": 0.74,\n      \"target_admin3_power\": 0.7,\n      \"target_met\": false,\n      \"admin_3_power_delta14\": 0.82,\n      \"fpr_cumulative\": 0.048,\n      \"fpr_stable_across_admins\": true,\n      \"bayes_factor_median_admin3\": 4.2,\n      \"simulation_n_items\": 500,\n      \"simulation_n_models_per_admin\": 200,\n      \"computation_time_hours\": 6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Cumulative Power by Administration\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"n_admins\",\n          \"power_delta_10\",\n          \"power_delta_14\",\n          \"power_delta_16\",\n          \"fpr\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            1,\n            0.41,\n            0.68,\n            0.72,\n            0.042\n          ],\n          [\n            2,\n            0.56,\n            0.77,\n            0.83,\n            0.045\n          ],\n          [\n            3,\n            0.68,\n            0.82,\n            0.89,\n            0.048\n          ],\n          [\n            4,\n            0.74,\n            0.86,\n            0.92,\n            0.047\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_007 有 modest value 作为 forward-looking contribution。 核心问题：ML 评审对 \\\"future benchmark administrations\\\" 的 temporal framing 不熟悉——psychometrics 中 repeated test administration 是常态， 但 LLM benchmarks 通常是 one-shot。需要明确解释 \\\"as new model generations emerge, the same benchmark is effectively re-administered\\\"。 Appendix 放置，主文 limitations 中一句话提及 cumulative power improvement 可能性。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：simulation 结果方向正确但 target 未达。 1) 3 次 administration 后 δ=1.0 的 power 从 0.41 升至 0.68——接近但未达 0.70 target。 δ=1.4 时 0.82 是可用的，说明 cumulative approach 有价值但主要对 medium effects。 2) FPR 控制良好 (0.048)，Bayesian prior 没有引入 FPR inflation。 3) 核心限制：这是 pure simulation，没有 real data validation。 METABENCH 只有一个 \\\"administration\\\"（没有 temporal sub-cohorts fine enough for 4 successive periods）。 4) Median 档评审：\\\"simulation-only result without empirical validation; interesting but speculative\\\"。 策略：appendix material。展示 concept 可行性但承认需要真实数据验证。 如果 ICLR 评审不熟悉 Bayesian DIF，这部分可能被完全忽略。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"graceful_degradation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"分析 benchmark validity 在 progressive item replacement 下的退化模式。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"replacement_5pct_rho\": 0.998,\n      \"replacement_10pct_rho\": 0.995,\n      \"replacement_20pct_rho\": 0.987,\n      \"replacement_50pct_rho\": 0.961,\n      \"reliability_5pct_alpha\": 0.943,\n      \"reliability_10pct_alpha\": 0.938,\n      \"reliability_20pct_alpha\": 0.924,\n      \"reliability_50pct_alpha\": 0.891,\n      \"original_alpha\": 0.946,\n      \"construct_coverage_20pct_subjects_lost\": 0,\n      \"construct_coverage_50pct_subjects_lost\": 3,\n      \"validity_floor_replacement_pct\": 0.35,\n      \"validity_floor_criterion\": \"ρ > 0.98 AND α > 0.92\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Validity Metrics Under Progressive Replacement\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"replacement_pct\",\n          \"rank_ρ\",\n          \"cronbach_α\",\n          \"subjects_under_represented\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0,\n            1.0,\n            0.946,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            5,\n            0.998,\n            0.943,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            10,\n            0.995,\n            0.938,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            20,\n            0.987,\n            0.924,\n            0\n          ],\n          [\n            35,\n            0.974,\n            0.908,\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            50,\n            0.961,\n            0.891,\n            3\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_008 的主要贡献是量化 \\\"how much replacement is safe\\\"—— 35% validity floor 直接对应 \\\"31% DIF items can be safely replaced without validity loss\\\"。这 strengthens the \\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\" narrative。 但 plan_006 的 negative result 使得 \\\"replacement\\\" 变成 theoretical exercise。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：graceful degradation 结果 clean 且 informative。 1) ρ 从 0.998 (5%) 到 0.961 (50%) 的退化曲线非常 smooth——MMLU 的 12,508 items 有 massive redundancy，即使替换 50% items 排名仍 strongly correlated。 这 complements plan_017 (ρ=0.997 after removing 31% DIF items)。 2) Reliability (Cronbach's α) 从 0.946 到 0.891——20% 是 practical threshold， 之后 reliability 下降加速。 3) Construct coverage：50% replacement 时 3 个 subjects 可能 under-represented (small subjects with few items)。 4) 核心问题：replacement 假设 generated items 质量 OK——但 plan_006 显示 generation 质量不足。所以 \\\"graceful degradation\\\" 只在理论层面成立。 Median 档评审：\\\"nice analysis but moot without better item generation (plan_006 failed)\\\"。 策略：clean supplementary result，放 appendix。主文用 \\\"validity floor at ~35% replacement\\\" 作为 practical recommendation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"item_focused_trees\",\n    \"description\": \"Tutz & Berger (2016) Item-Focused Trees 作为 categorical DIF 的替代方案。 Treat model release date as continuous covariate。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_items_analyzed\": 12508,\n      \"n_items_with_significant_split\": 4127,\n      \"pct_items_with_split\": 33.0,\n      \"primary_split_date\": \"2023-11-15\",\n      \"concordance_with_mh_ets_c\": 0.78,\n      \"additional_items_detected\": 209,\n      \"items_missed_by_ift\": 612,\n      \"jaccard_mh_vs_ift\": 0.68,\n      \"computational_time_hours\": 12,\n      \"n_items_nonlinear_trend\": 1834,\n      \"pct_nonlinear\": 14.7\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: MH vs IFT Concordance\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"mh_ets_c\",\n          \"ift_significant\",\n          \"overlap\",\n          \"jaccard\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"n_flagged\",\n            3918,\n            4127,\n            3306,\n            0.68\n          ],\n          [\n            \"pct_flagged\",\n            31.3,\n            33.0,\n            26.4,\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_009 的 concordance=0.78 有两面性： - 支持：MH 的 categorical split 不是 artifact，IFT confirms temporal instability - 质疑：22% discordance 说明 method choice matters，results are partially method-dependent 评审在 median 档接受 IFT 作为 robustness check，不会深入追究 discordance。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：IFT 是有价值的 robustness check 但不改变 narrative。 1) 33% items with significant split vs MH 31.3%——high concordance (0.78)， 说明 categorical temporal split 不是 arbitrary 的。 2) Primary split date 2023-11-15——接近 GPT-4/Llama-2 到 Llama-3/Mixtral 的代际转换点，有 face validity。 3) IFT detects 209 additional items that MH misses (mostly items with gradual drift rather than sharp shift)，同时 misses 612 items MH catches (mostly items where DIF is large but not monotone in date)。 4) 14.7% nonlinear trends——说明 some items 的 DIF 不是 monotone temporal， 暗示 \\\"contamination + capability gain + item drift\\\" 的 multi-factor story。 Median 档评审：\\\"useful supplementary analysis, confirms MH results are not artifacts of the cohort split\\\"。不改变 claims 但提供 methodological robustness。 策略：appendix 的 robustness check。主文一句话：\\\"IFT with continuous release date yields 78% concordance with MH categorical DIF (Appendix X)\\\"。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"architecture_stratified_dif\",\n    \"description\": \"在 decoder-only 子群内重跑 DIF，检验 architecture heterogeneity 是否影响 IRT fit。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_decoder_only\": 5226,\n      \"n_non_decoder\": 1,\n      \"pct_decoder_only\": 99.98,\n      \"decoder_only_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"full_population_c_pct\": 31.3,\n      \"jaccard_decoder_vs_full\": 1.0,\n      \"irt_rmsea_full\": 0.089,\n      \"irt_rmsea_decoder_only\": 0.088,\n      \"irt_cfi_full\": 0.72,\n      \"irt_cfi_decoder_only\": 0.72,\n      \"irt_fit_improvement\": \"negligible\",\n      \"pct_models_lz_gt2\": 98.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Architecture Stratification Results\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"population\",\n          \"n_models\",\n          \"c_pct\",\n          \"rmsea\",\n          \"cfi\",\n          \"pct_lz_gt2\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"full\",\n            5227,\n            31.3,\n            0.089,\n            0.72,\n            98.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"decoder-only\",\n            5226,\n            31.3,\n            0.088,\n            0.72,\n            98.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"delta\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.0,\n            0.001,\n            0.0,\n            0.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_010 的 value 是 defensive：排除一个 potential confound。 但它也暴露了真正的问题——IRT misfit 来自 multidimensionality， 这正是评审的 attack vector。Plan_005 bifactor pilot 是 partial response， 但 median 档下不够 convincing (CFI=0.81)。 最佳回应策略：承认 misspecification，展示 DIF 发现在 bifactor 校正后 qualitatively 不变 (C% ~28-29% vs 31.3%)，argue \\\"our findings are conservative estimates\\\"。\\n\\n\\nMedian 档：plan_010 是 clean knockout result。 1) METABENCH MMLU 是 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227)——removing 1 non-decoder model changes literally nothing (Jaccard=1.0)。 2) IRT fit 不改善 (RMSEA 0.089→0.088, CFI 0.72→0.72)——因为 misfit 来自 MMLU 的 57-subject multidimensionality，不是 architecture heterogeneity。 3) 98% models 有 |Lz|>2——这反映 1D IRT 对 MMLU 的 fundamental misspecification， 不是 population heterogeneity。 Median 档评审接受这个 null result：architecture 不是问题。但会转向 \\\"OK so the misfit is from multidimensionality, have you tried multidimensional IRT?\\\"—— 这是 median 档的核心 concern 之一。 策略：主文用一段报告 99.98% decoder-only + Jaccard=1.0。 IRT fit 数据放 limitations 讨论，作为 multidimensional IRT future work 的动机。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"向真实 METABENCH response matrix 注入已知 contamination，测量 DIF 检测力。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"n_clean_items\": 500,\n      \"n_injected_items\": 200,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p0\": 0.326,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p03\": 0.548,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p05\": 0.834,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p07\": 0.99,\n      \"temporal_external_tpr_p10\": 1.0,\n      \"temporal_external_fpr\": 0.314,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05\": 0.508,\n      \"temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.674,\n      \"ability_external_delta_tpr_p10\": 0.302,\n      \"cross_subject_delta_fpr\": 0.0,\n      \"within_subject_fpr_inflation_p10\": 0.186,\n      \"dose_response_monotone\": true,\n      \"dose_response_p_values\": [\n        0.3,\n        0.5,\n        0.7,\n        1.0\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Semi-synthetic Detection Power (Cross-subject Matching)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"exploitation_rate_p\",\n          \"baseline_tpr\",\n          \"injected_tpr\",\n          \"delta_tpr\",\n          \"fpr\",\n          \"delta_fpr\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.0 (no injection)\",\n            0.326,\n            0.326,\n            0.0,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            0.3,\n            0.326,\n            0.548,\n            0.222,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            0.326,\n            0.834,\n            0.508,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            0.7,\n            0.326,\n            0.99,\n            0.664,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            1.0,\n            0.326,\n            1.0,\n            0.674,\n            0.314,\n            0.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: Within-subject vs Cross-subject Matching\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"matching\",\n          \"delta_tpr_p05\",\n          \"delta_fpr_p10\",\n          \"fpr_stable\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"within-subject\",\n            0.457,\n            0.186,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"cross-subject\",\n            0.508,\n            0.0,\n            true\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Median 档下 plan_011 (+plan_016 cross-subject replication) 是 Claim 3 的 robust foundation。Reviewers 在 median 档给 semi-synthetic framework positive marks (novelty sub-score 2.5 on this specific contribution)。 唯一 downside：injection simplicity。Rebuttal 准备： \\\"Our injection flips incorrect→correct, which is the minimal model of contamination (memorized answer). More complex patterns (partial memorization, verbatim recall) would produce LARGER DIF effects, not smaller—our power estimates are conservative.\\\"\\n\\nMedian 档：plan_011 是 paper 的 strongest evidence 之一。 1) ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5 是 clean, large effect——从 baseline 0.326 升至 0.834， 明确证明 DIF 能 detect injected differential contamination。 2) Dose-response 从 p=0.3 到 p=1.0 monotone——mechanistic validation。 3) Cross-subject matching ΔFPR=0.000 是 key innovation——完全消除 FPR inflation， vs within-subject matching +0.186。这是 Claim 3 的核心证据。 4) Baseline FPR=0.314 (= temporal C%=31.3%)——评审会问 \\\"is 31% baseline FPR acceptable?\\\" Answer: this IS the real DIF rate, not false positives. Semi-synthetic 只 adds signal on top of real baseline。 Median 档评审对 plan_011 的质疑集中在： - \\\"injection mechanism (incorrect→correct) is simplistic—real contamination\\n  may produce different patterns (e.g., faster response time, different error types)\\\"\\n- \\\"you inject into real matrices, but the contamination is still artificial\\\" 这些是 acknowledged limitations，不是 fatal flaws。 策略：plan_011 在主文 §4 占重要位置。Cross-subject matching 作为 methodological recommendation 明确 highlight。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":924,"startLine":1,"totalLines":924}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01THhuWDt9U4PUCdwZw3nf3u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive understanding of the experiment data and paper framing. Let me also check the paper-writing-norms skill and the existing paper for LaTeX style reference.\n\nLet me now write the full paper. I need to cover:\n\n1. Abstract\n2. Introduction\n3. Related Work (brief)\n4. Method (MH-DIF, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\n5. Experiments (covering all experiments from experiment_data.json)\n6. Discussion + Limitations\n7. Conclusion\n\nThe experiments from experiment_data.json are:\n1. real_data_dif_mmlu - Main DIF analysis (Table 1, Table 2)\n\n\n2. rl_robustness_validation - RL robustness (appendix)\n3. constat_perturbation_eval - ConStat comparison (appendix)\n4. dvd_generation_variance_eval - DVD comparison (appendix)\n5. ensemble_fusion - Ensemble (appendix)\n6. cross_benchmark_gsm8k - GSM8K cross-benchmark (main + appendix)\n7. bifactor_irt_equating_pilot - Bifactor IRT (appendix)\n8. item_generation_calibration - Item generation (appendix)\n9. cumulative_bayesian_dif - Bayesian DIF (appendix)\n10. graceful_degradation_analysis - Degradation (appendix)\n11. item_focused_trees - IFT robustness (appendix)\n12. architecture_stratified_dif - Architecture check (main, brief)\n13. semi_synthetic_contamination_validation - Semi-synthetic (main)\n\nI need to ensure each experiment gets its own section or table entry. The main paper will focus on Claims 1-4 with the primary experiments, while the appendix handles all the supporting analyses. Now I'm ready to start writing the full LaTeX document.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5947,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15864,"cache_read_input_tokens":23745,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15864},"output_tokens"